Re:Kernel kernel integration (drivers/rekernel + binder/signal hooks)

Sourced from https://github.com/Sakion-Team/Re-Kernel (main, Integrate/;
rekernel.c/rekernel.h/Kconfig/Makefile are identical in the ReKernel-X
upstream/v9.2 fork), adapted for the LineageOS 4.9.337 base:

- drivers/rekernel/{Kconfig,Makefile,rekernel.c,rekernel.h} verbatim
  (GPL-2.0), with CONFIG_REKERNEL=y / CONFIG_REKERNEL_NETWORK=y;
- drivers/android/binder.c: frozen-process async transaction handling
  (binder_can_update_transaction()/
  binder_find_outdated_transaction_ilocked()) plus the
  rekernel_binder_transaction() netlink report hook before
  trace_binder_transaction(). The upstream patches.sh variant keys the
  merge on TF_UPDATE_TXN (binder update transactions, 4.14+); this tree
  has no TF_UPDATE_TXN, so the merge applies to every async transaction
  of a frozen process (ReKernel-X v9.2 wording) and drops the fields
  that do not exist here (binder_buffer->pid, proc->outstanding_txns);
- kernel/signal.c: rekernel_report(SIGNAL, ...) for SIGKILL/SIGTERM/
  SIGABRT/SIGQUIT in do_send_sig_info();
- drivers/Kconfig + drivers/Makefile wiring.

4.9 adaptation: JOBCTL_TRAP_FREEZE does not exist before 4.11, so
jobctl_frozen() falls back to frozen()/freezing() from freezer.h.
